                            <div class="outcome-text"><strong>E1(i):</strong> <del>On a daily basis, Amelia will be able to independently initiate conversations with both trusted adults and peers across diverse environments, such as educational and social settings. This interaction will encompass not only casual conversation but also the proactive seeking of assistance or clarification through questions.</del><br><br><strong><em>SMART Revision: By [end of term/specific date], Amelia will independently initiate at least [3] conversations per day with trusted adults and/or peers in educational settings, increasing from current baseline of [X] initiations per day. Initiations will include both social conversation (at least [1] per day) and help-seeking/clarification requests (at least [1] per day), as tracked by daily observation logs. Success will be measured by frequency of initiations, independence level (unprompted), and range of communication partners (minimum [2] different adults and [2] different peers per week).</em></strong><br><br><strong>E1(ii):</strong> <del>Amelia will be able to observe examples of social interaction between others (using video, cartoon strips and scripts) and identify/explain at least 2 positive and 2 negative behaviours which support or hinder the success of the communication.</del><br><br><strong><em>SMART Revision: By [end of term/specific date], when presented with [10] video/visual examples of social interactions, Amelia will correctly identify and explain at least 2 positive and 2 negative communication behaviours in 8 out of 10 scenarios (80% accuracy), improving from current baseline of [X/10] correct responses. Explanations must demonstrate understanding of why behaviours support or hinder communication, as assessed by [specific rubric/criteria]. Progress will be reviewed [monthly/termly] using standardized social scenarios.</em></strong><br><br><strong>E2:</strong> <del>Amelia will be able to participate in small group activities with up to three peers who share similar interests and hobbies, for 20 minutes, three times weekly.</del><br><br><strong><em>SMART Revision: By [end of term/specific date], Amelia will successfully participate in small group activities (2-3 peers with shared interests) for 20 minutes, 3 times per week, increasing from current baseline of [X minutes/Y times per week]. Success will be measured by: (1) duration of participation without needing breaks, (2) quality of participation (making at least [2] relevant contributions per session), (3) emotional regulation maintained throughout (no distress episodes), and (4) self-reported enjoyment rating of [X/10] or higher. Progress tracked via weekly observation forms completed by supervising adult.</em></strong></div>
