                            <span class="label label-need">NEED 8</span>
                            <div class="need-text">Amelia's receptive language skills are mixed. Whilst core skills are secure, Amelia can find it harder to understand the more nuanced and abstract content of spoken language. She tends to interpret what she hears literally, finding it harder to understand subtle, inferred language and ambiguity, this impacting on her success at "reading" situations and leading to social vulnerability, confusion and anxiety.</div>
                            <span class="label label-outcome">Outcomes</span>
                            <div class="outcome-text"><strong>E1(iii):</strong> <del>Amelia will be able to observe examples of social interaction between others (using video, cartoon strips and scripts) and identify examples of sarcasm, irony, inference, slang, metaphorical language and figurative terms and explain the reason for their use.</del><br><br><strong><em>SMART Revision: By [end of term/specific date], Amelia will correctly identify and explain sarcasm, irony, inference, slang, metaphorical language, and figurative terms in 8 out of 10 (80%) observed social interaction examples (video, cartoon strips, scripts), improving from current baseline of [X/10] correct identifications. Additionally, in authentic communication contexts, Amelia will demonstrate comprehension of figurative/inferred language directed at her by providing appropriate responses in [6 out of 10] (60%) naturalistic situations, as measured by role-play scenarios and real-time observations tracked [weekly/monthly]. Progress will include both identification accuracy and real-world application, with targets adjusted based on language complexity level.</em></strong><br><br><em>Note: This outcome is weak as it only addresses identification and explanation of nuanced language through observation of others, rather than demonstrating comprehension and appropriate response to these language features in real-time social interactions. A stronger outcome would measure Amelia's ability to interpret and respond appropriately to figurative and inferred language when it is directed at her in authentic communication contexts.</em></div>
